The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (vport->enabled) {
    ...
} else {
    NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(extack, "Eswitch vport is disabled");
}
```
Reason:
The code checks if the vport is enabled and attempts to set an error message in the `extack` variable when the vport is disabled. This is inappropriate because querying the hardware address of a disabled vport is unsupported and should not trigger an error log.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (vport->enabled) {
    ether_addr_copy(hw_addr, vport->info.mac);
    *hw_addr_len = ETH_ALEN;
    err = 0;
} 
// Removed else block that sets the error message
```
Reason:
The patch removes the else block that sets the error message for a disabled vport, thus preventing the logging of an error when querying the hardware address of a disabled vport, which is the correct behavior since such a query is unsupported.

